    "_id": "demoCareerUniver",
    "name": "Demo — Harbour University",
    "type": "career",
    "img": "icons/svg/book.svg",
    "flags": {
        "mgt2": {
            "demo": {
                "order": 38,
                "cliff": "an education is a career Item that runs a different set of rolls",
                "teaches": [
                    "A university has no tied career: its skills come from its own Service Skills table, and each pick says how many rows to take and at what level.",
                    "A pick's Level is the level the skill ends at; blank takes the row as printed, so one pick at level 0 and one at level 1 give the book's 'a level 0 and a level 1 skill' and neither a blank nor a 0 on the second pick will do.",
                    "Graduation raises what the education gave by one level (the raise block), grants EDU, and leaves a DM+1 to qualify for each named career, DM+1 more with honours.",
                    "Honours also leave a DM+2 on the commission roll before the first term of the first career after the school, held until that roll is made."
                ],
                "trap": "The university teaches from its own tables.service, so that table is filled in, unlike the cadet school's tied one; the other three tables, the ladders, assignments and benefits stay empty because an education never reads them. The fail arm is empty by decision: a graduate who fails keeps the skills and gains nothing else. The Harbour Patrol never commissions, so the honours commission DM stays pending when it is the first career entered. The eleven record fields below the tables stay empty, as on every template."
            }
        }
    },
